192
00:16:17.102 --> 00:16:21.396
KATE: Yeah. Yeah, you're right.
You're right. We're fine.

193
00:16:21.899 --> 00:16:23.891
PETER:
Nothing to worry about.

194
00:16:43.378 --> 00:16:44.754
Mom?

195
00:16:46.256 --> 00:16:47.667
Dad?

196
00:16:48.759 --> 00:16:50.383
Uncle Frank?

197
00:16:51.929 --> 00:16:53.091
Buzz?

198
00:17:01.355 --> 00:17:03.513
We're the last ones off the plane.

199
00:17:08.195 --> 00:17:10.484
Where are those guys?

200
00:17:16.453 --> 00:17:18.173
PETER: Is this Megan's?
KATE: It's Brooke's.

201
00:17:18.413 --> 00:17:21.664
Give this to Brooke, this to Kevin.

202
00:17:21.875 --> 00:17:24.876
- Give this... Give this to Kevin.
- Give this to Kevin.

203
00:17:25.087 --> 00:17:26.249
Give this to Kevin.

204
00:17:26.463 --> 00:17:27.542
- Kevin.
- Kevin.

205
00:17:27.798 --> 00:17:29.921
- Give this to Kevin.
- Give this to Kevin.

206
00:17:30.175 --> 00:17:32.132
- Give this to Kevin.
- Kevin.

207
00:17:32.386 --> 00:17:35.007
- Give this to Kevin.
- Here you go, Kevin.

208
00:17:42.145 --> 00:17:44.637
- Kevin's not here.
- Kevin's not here.

209
00:17:44.857 --> 00:17:47.312
- Kevin's not here.
- Kevin's not here.

210
00:17:47.526 --> 00:17:50.064
- Kevin's not here.
- Kevin's not here.

211
00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.776
- Kevin's not here.
- Kevin's not here.

212
00:17:53.031 --> 00:17:54.442
Kevin's not here.

213
00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:56.277
Kevin's not here.

214
00:17:57.536 --> 00:17:58.781
What!

215
00:18:02.541 --> 00:18:04.000
Kevin!

216
00:18:27.441 --> 00:18:28.639
(GASPS)

217
00:18:32.196 --> 00:18:34.354
Excuse me, this is an emergency!

218
00:18:36.158 --> 00:18:37.154
Yes, sir?

219
00:18:37.367 --> 00:18:38.648
What city is that?

220
00:18:40.996 --> 00:18:42.194
That's New York.

221
00:18:43.248 --> 00:18:45.205
Yikes, I did it again!

222
00:18:50.255 --> 00:18:51.536
Something wrong, sir?

223
00:18:54.885 --> 00:18:56.545
I'll be fine.

224
00:19:05.812 --> 00:19:10.309
Oh, no. My family's in Florida
and I'm in New York.

225
00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:14.813
My family's in Florida?

226
00:19:15.072 --> 00:19:16.352
I'm in...

227
00:19:17.074 --> 00:19:18.865
New York?

228
00:20:28.604 --> 00:20:30.181
Wow.

229
00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:06.182
What's the child's name?

230
00:21:06.391 --> 00:21:09.096
- Kevin.
- K-E-V-l-N.

231
00:21:09.311 --> 00:21:11.268
When did you see him last?

232
00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:12.511
Curbside check-in?

233
00:21:12.773 --> 00:21:16.058
No, I saw him at the door.
He was with us in the terminal.

234
00:21:17.194 --> 00:21:21.820
Most people get separated at security.
Did everyone get through security?

235
00:21:22.032 --> 00:21:23.989
I don't know. Peter...

236
00:21:24.243 --> 00:21:27.078
We were in a hurry.
We ran all the way to the gate.

237
00:21:27.621 --> 00:21:30.373
When did you notice he was missing?

238
00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:34.001
When we picked up our baggage here.

239
00:21:34.837 --> 00:21:37.790
- Has the boy ever run away from home?
- No.

240
00:21:38.006 --> 00:21:40.758
Has he ever been in a situation
on his own?

241
00:21:45.973 --> 00:21:48.677
As a matter of fact,
this has happened before.

242
00:21:49.309 --> 00:21:52.476
KATE: It's becoming a McCallister
family travel tradition.

243
00:21:53.564 --> 00:21:56.933
Funnily enough,
we never lose our luggage.

244
00:21:58.443 --> 00:21:59.938
(KNOCKING)

245
00:22:08.662 --> 00:22:12.161
He was left at home,
by accident, last year.

246
00:22:13.208 --> 00:22:18.001
That's what my wife meant calling it
a McCallister family travel tradition.

247
00:22:19.756 --> 00:22:21.464
We'll call Chicago and...

248
00:22:21.717 --> 00:22:23.959
notify them of the situation.

249
00:22:24.219 --> 00:22:26.544
The odds are that's where he is.

250
00:22:27.306 --> 00:22:28.136
Thanks.

251
00:22:29.016 --> 00:22:31.767
Very unlikely he'd be anywhere else.

252
00:22:44.948 --> 00:22:46.490
(HORN HONKS)

253
00:22:46.742 --> 00:22:48.450
DRIVER:
Watch out, kid!

254
00:23:01.048 --> 00:23:03.087
WORKER:
Yo, where's your manifest?

