- That's very responsible of you.

512
00:47:10.497 --> 00:47:11.908
Oh, well, thank you.

513
00:47:12.165 --> 00:47:13.624
My pleasure.

514
00:47:13.876 --> 00:47:18.372
That'll be $23.75.

515
00:47:20.007 --> 00:47:22.628
My, my, my.
Where did you get all that money?

516
00:47:24.887 --> 00:47:27.128
- I have a lot of grandmothers.
- Oh.

517
00:47:27.806 --> 00:47:29.431
Well, that explains it.

518
00:47:31.560 --> 00:47:35.889
This is a nice store. One of the
finer toy dealerships I've visited.

519
00:47:36.106 --> 00:47:37.137
Well, thank you.

520
00:47:37.357 --> 00:47:39.315
Mr. Duncan must be a nice guy...

521
00:47:39.526 --> 00:47:42.611
letting kids come in here
and play with his toys.

522
00:47:42.863 --> 00:47:44.772
Most toy stores prohibit that.

523
00:47:44.990 --> 00:47:46.153
- Is that so?
- Yes.

524
00:47:46.408 --> 00:47:48.650
Well, he loves kids.

525
00:47:48.911 --> 00:47:53.039
As a matter of fact, all the money
the store takes in today...

526
00:47:53.290 --> 00:47:56.457
Mr. Duncan is donating
to the Children's Hospital.

527
00:47:56.668 --> 00:47:58.791
And the day after Christmas...

528
00:47:59.004 --> 00:48:02.171
we empty out all the money
in the cash register...

529
00:48:02.382 --> 00:48:05.549
and Mr. Duncan takes it
right down to the hospital.

530
00:48:05.928 --> 00:48:07.208
That's generous of him.

531
00:48:07.429 --> 00:48:10.763
Well, children bring him
a lot of joy...

532
00:48:11.016 --> 00:48:14.266
as they do to everyone
who appreciates them.

533
00:48:19.983 --> 00:48:24.941
I'm not supposed to spend this, but
I have $20 in a jar in our garage...

534
00:48:25.155 --> 00:48:29.105
where my brother can't find it.
So I can pay my mother back.

535
00:48:29.368 --> 00:48:33.365
So give this to Mr. Duncan.
The hospital needs it more than I do.

536
00:48:33.580 --> 00:48:38.159
Besides, I'll probably spend it on
stuff that will rot my teeth and mind.

537
00:48:40.838 --> 00:48:44.289
Ah, that's...
That's very sweet of you.

538
00:48:45.217 --> 00:48:47.256
You see that tree there?

539
00:48:47.511 --> 00:48:51.176
Well, to show our appreciation
for your generosity...

540
00:48:51.390 --> 00:48:54.095
I'll let you select an object
from that tree...

541
00:48:54.309 --> 00:48:57.429
to take home with you.
- For free?

542
00:48:58.564 --> 00:49:01.518
- May I make a suggestion?
- Okay.

543
00:49:01.733 --> 00:49:03.856
Take the turtledoves.

544
00:49:04.486 --> 00:49:05.815
I can have two?

545
00:49:06.029 --> 00:49:10.407
Well, "two turtledoves."
And I tell you what you do.

546
00:49:10.659 --> 00:49:12.237
You keep one...

547
00:49:12.661 --> 00:49:16.445
and give the other one
to a very special person.

548
00:49:17.040 --> 00:49:18.914
You see, turtledoves...

549
00:49:19.418 --> 00:49:22.454
are a symbol of friendship
and love.

550
00:49:22.754 --> 00:49:26.206
Now, as long as each of you
have your turtledove...

551
00:49:26.466 --> 00:49:29.040
you'll be friends forever.

552
00:49:29.303 --> 00:49:33.466
Wow, I never knew that. I thought
they were just part of a song.

553
00:49:33.682 --> 00:49:37.466
They are. And for that
very special reason.

554
00:49:38.520 --> 00:49:39.469
Wow.

555
00:49:39.855 --> 00:49:40.851
Thanks.

556
00:49:41.106 --> 00:49:42.351
Merry Christmas.

557
00:49:42.566 --> 00:49:44.559
Merry Christmas to you too.

558
00:49:44.860 --> 00:49:47.647
Be sure to bundle up if you
go outside. It's nippy.

559
00:49:48.488 --> 00:49:50.980
Oh. I'll do that.

560
00:50:27.903 --> 00:50:29.611
Well, where to?

561
00:50:30.072 --> 00:50:32.907
You promised you'd take me
to the Central Park Zoo.

562
00:50:41.375 --> 00:50:43.996
Hey, look who it is.

563
00:50:47.631 --> 00:50:49.339
Come on, let's get him.

564
00:50:55.222 --> 00:50:56.385
HARRY:
Hi, pal.

565
00:51:03.063 --> 00:51:04.438
(GASPS)

566
00:51:04.815 --> 00:51:06.143
(SCREAMS)

567
00:51:15.993 --> 00:51:17.155
Come on.

568
00:51:32.676 --> 00:51:34.051
MAN 1:
Hey!

569
00:51:39.349 --> 00:51:40.760
MAN 2:
Hey, watch it, man!

570
00:51:41.018 --> 00:51:42.560
(GLASS BREAKS)

571
00:51:42.978 --> 00:51:47.391
Buy now and avoid the Christmas rush.
Two for $5. Two for $5.

572
00:51:47.858 --> 00:51:49.269
Four for 10.

573
00:51:49.735 --> 00:51:50.897
There he is!

574
00:51:51.445 --> 00:51:52.524
All right.

575
00:51:53.488 --> 00:51:55.730
- Thanks.
- Merry Christmas, dude.

576
00:52:25.229 --> 00:52:26.771
BOTH:
Whoa!

577
00:52:29.525 --> 00:52:30.639
Oh...

578
00:52:32.110 --> 00:52:33.486
Yes!

579
00:52:33.862 --> 00:52:37.196
WOMAN: Thank you for your suggestion.
CONCIERGE: My duty. My pleasure.

580
00:52:49.002 --> 00:52:51.291
Help! There's two guys after me!

581
00:52:51.880 --> 00:52:55.380
What's the matter?
Store wouldn't take your...

582
00:52:55.968 --> 00:52:58.007
stolen credit card?

583
00:52:58.929 --> 00:53:01.883
Let's see what the police
have to say about this.

584
00:53:07.729 --> 00:53:09.354
HARRY:
Get up! Get up!

585
00:53:10.691 --> 00:53:12.315
Come on! Let's go get him.

586
00:53:14.444 --> 00:53:17.114
Get back here, you little thief!

587
00:53:20.033 --> 00:53:21.113
Stop that child!

588
00:53:24.997 --> 00:53:26.242
Grab him!

589
00:53:31.170 --> 00:53:32.996
Whoa!

590
00:53:35.757 --> 00:53:37.300
(GROANING)

591
00:53:41.096 --> 00:53:42.923
You little sh...

592
00:53:44.975 --> 00:53:47.217
I've committed credit card fraud.

593
00:53:47.436 --> 00:53:49.393
CONCIERGE:
Get me security!

594
00:53:49.605 --> 00:53:52.641
We've got to stop that delinquent!

595
00:53:52.900 --> 00:53:55.854
Come along, Cedric!

596
00:54:14.087 --> 00:54:17.421
I've had enough of this vacation.
I'm going home.

597
00:54:28.769 --> 00:54:29.682
Hold it!

598
00:54:31.897 --> 00:54:33.640
This is the Concierge, sir!

599
00:54:34.942 --> 00:54:36.650
I knew it was you.

600
00:54:36.902 --> 00:54:38.978
I could smell you
getting off the elevator.

601
00:54:41.740 --> 00:54:43.863
JOHNNY: You was here last night too,
wasn 't you?

602
00:54:46.161 --> 00:54:48.201
Yes, sir.

603
00:54:48.413 --> 00:54:49.279
I was.

604
00:54:49.915 --> 00:54:53.165
You was here and you was smooching
with my brother.

605
00:54:54.086 --> 00:54:55.710
Bu...

606
00:54:56.922 --> 00:54:58.582
You're mistaken, sir.

607
00:54:59.341 --> 00:55:02.176
Don 't give me that.
You've smooched everybody.

608
00:55:02.511 --> 00:55:06.888
Snuffy, Al, Leo, Little Moe
with the gimpy leg...

609
00:55:07.224 --> 00:55:09.347
Cheeks, Boney Bob, Cliff...

610
00:55:09.810 --> 00:55:10.640
(GASPS)

611
00:55:12.479 --> 00:55:14.271
No!

612
00:55:16.024 --> 00:55:17.519
It's a lie!

613
00:55:17.734 --> 00:55:20.107
JOHNNY:
I could go on forever, baby.

614
00:55:20.612 --> 00:55:23.234
I'm terribly sorry, sir.

615
00:55:23.448 --> 00:55:25.108
I'm afraid you're mistaken.

616
00:55:25.742 --> 00:55:27.450
We're looking for a young man.

617
00:55:27.703 --> 00:55:30.158
All right, I believe you...

618
00:55:30.414 --> 00:55:31.872
but my Tommy gun don 't.

619
00:55:32.124 --> 00:55:33.203
(GASPS)

620
00:55:33.417 --> 00:55:36.086
Get down on your knees
and tell me you love me.

621
00:55:39.339 --> 00:55:40.750
On your knees.

622
00:55:49.600 --> 00:55:52.007
I love you!

623
00:55:52.644 --> 00:55:54.554
(LAUGHS)

624
00:55:55.230 --> 00:55:56.890
You gotta do better than that!

625
00:55:58.609 --> 00:56:00.648
I love you!

626
00:56:02.529 --> 00:56:04.107
JOHNNY:
Maybe I'm off my hinges...

627
00:56:04.573 --> 00:56:05.604
but I believe you.

628
00:56:05.866 --> 00:56:08.273
That's why I'm gonna let you go.

629
00:56:09.161 --> 00:56:13.159
I'm gonna give you till the count
of three to get your lousy...

630
00:56:13.665 --> 00:56:15.658
lying, low-down...

631
00:56:15.876 --> 00:56:18.331
four-flushing carcass out my door!

632
00:56:20.422 --> 00:56:21.667
- One!
- Open the door!

633
00:56:21.924 --> 00:56:22.789
Two!

634
00:56:25.427 --> 00:56:27.420
(GUNFIRE ON TV)

635
00:56:37.439 --> 00:56:38.814
Three.

636
00:56:39.233 --> 00:56:42.269
JOHNNY:
Merry Christmas, you filthy animal.

637
00:56:44.821 --> 00:56:46.861
JOHNNY:
And a happy new year.

638
00:56:49.368 --> 00:56:52.203
Stay in your rooms!
This is an emergency!

639
00:56:52.871 --> 00:56:56.240
There's an insane guest with a gun!

640
00:57:06.718 --> 00:57:08.094
No!

641
00:57:11.431 --> 00:57:13.341
Come to Papa!

642
00:57:15.310 --> 00:57:18.975
Round trip to Miami. What's the
matter, get on the wrong plane?

643
00:57:19.231 --> 00:57:20.974
You won't be needing this.

644
00:57:21.233 --> 00:57:25.444
American don't fly to the
promised land, little buddy.

645
00:57:27.364 --> 00:57:31.528
We spent 9 months in jail thinking
we had the worst luck in the universe.

646
00:57:31.785 --> 00:57:33.196
We were wrong.

647
00:57:33.453 --> 00:57:36.953
We busted out and we're doing fine.
Even better...

648
00:57:37.207 --> 00:57:40.623
because we're not robbing houses,
we're robbing toy stores.

649
00:57:40.836 --> 00:57:44.003
At midnight tonight,
we'll hit Duncan's Toy Chest.

650
00:57:44.214 --> 00:57:45.922
Five floors of cash.

651
00:57:46.175 --> 00:57:49.757
Then after that, we grab some
phony passports and go to Rio.

652
00:57:50.012 --> 00:57:53.796
- You want to shut up?
- He's not gonna talk to anybody.

653
00:57:54.057 --> 00:57:56.097
Except maybe a fish.

654
00:57:56.310 --> 00:57:57.341
Or the undertaker.

655
00:57:57.603 --> 00:58:02.561
Let's go to the subway tunnel.
I'll feel better once I get him on ice.

656
00:58:04.735 --> 00:58:05.933
HARRY:
I've got a gun.

657
00:58:06.195 --> 00:58:09.860
Say anything and you'll be spitting
gum out through your forehead.

658
00:58:30.677 --> 00:58:31.507
Well, hello.

659
00:58:35.516 --> 00:58:36.511
He did it!

660
00:58:37.267 --> 00:58:38.299
Did what?

661
00:58:41.230 --> 00:58:42.605
Thanks!

662
00:58:45.817 --> 00:58:47.857
HARRY: Go get him.
MARV: He went in the park.

663
00:58:48.111 --> 00:58:49.903
HARRY:
What are you doing flirting?!

664
00:58:52.407 --> 00:58:55.159
(KIDS SHOUTING)

665
00:59:25.691 --> 00:59:26.805
Over there!

666
00:59:33.532 --> 00:59:35.359
BO Y: Don't!
GIRL: Give it!

667
00:59:36.702 --> 00:59:37.567
MARV:
Hey, Harry.

668
00:59:38.161 --> 00:59:39.442
- I got him.
- Let me see!

669
00:59:39.705 --> 00:59:42.575
That ain't him! Put him down.
That ain't him.

670
00:59:43.292 --> 00:59:47.621
We should've shot him. I hate pulling
a job, knowing that creep's loose.

671
00:59:47.838 --> 00:59:51.337
- What can he do? Kids are helpless.
- Not this kid.

672
00:59:51.592 --> 00:59:56.004
But this time he doesn't have a house
full of dangerous goodies.

673
00:59:56.221 --> 01:00:00.005
He's in the park. He's alone.
Kids are scared of the park.

674
01:00:00.225 --> 01:00:04.175
Yeah. Grown men come in the park
and don't leave alive.

675
01:00:05.480 --> 01:00:07.272
Good luck, little fella.

676
01:00:18.285 --> 01:00:19.993
KEVIN:
I want to go home.

677
01:00:20.787 --> 01:00:22.697
Mom, where are you?

678
01:00:23.665 --> 01:00:26.417
(THUNDER BOOMS)

679
01:00:26.710 --> 01:00:29.379
(SPEAKING IN SPANISH)

680
01:00:50.734 --> 01:00:52.145
(PHONE RINGS)

681
01:00:52.402 --> 01:00:53.731
Turn that down!

682
01:00:56.073 --> 01:00:57.273
- Hello?
COP: Kate McCallister.

683
01:00:57.366 --> 01:00:58.908
- This is she.
- We found him.

684
01:00:59.159 --> 01:01:00.618
- Oh, my God!
- What?

685
01:01:00.827 --> 01:01:02.785
- They know where Kevin is.
- Where?

686
01:01:03.038 --> 01:01:05.031
- He's in New York City.
- New York!

687
01:01:05.249 --> 01:01:06.494
New York?

688
01:01:08.210 --> 01:01:09.206
What?

689
01:01:09.920 --> 01:01:13.004
- He's scared, he's not a troublemaker.
- What? What?

690
01:01:13.215 --> 01:01:17.343
Just a second. He used your credit
card to check into the Plaza Hotel.

691
01:01:18.387 --> 01:01:20.047
- Do they have him?
- Is he there?

692
01:01:20.264 --> 01:01:22.552
- No, they're still looking.
- Damn it!

693
01:01:22.766 --> 01:01:25.304
- Get to New York.
- We're on the next flight out.

694
01:01:25.561 --> 01:01:27.767
Thanks.
We're going to New York, move it!

695
01:01:27.980 --> 01:01:29.178
Yes!

696
01:01:30.482 --> 01:01:34.432
He ran away when they asked about
the card. He must be scared!

697
01:01:34.945 --> 01:01:37.862
- Would he go to my brother's?
- Aren't they in Paris?

698
01:01:38.282 --> 01:01:41.733
- Maybe they have a housesitter.
- Aren't they renovating?

699
01:02:12.941 --> 01:02:14.601
(KNOCKING)

700
01:02:21.742 --> 01:02:23.236
Hello?!

701
01:02:24.161 --> 01:02:26.913
Uncle Rob! Aunt Georgette!

702
01:02:27.164 --> 01:02:29.073
Anybody home?!

703
01:02:29.917 --> 01:02:30.996
Hello!

704
01:02:31.585 --> 01:02:33.163
Anybody home?

705
01:02:33.420 --> 01:02:36.172
It's me, your favorite nephew, Kevin!

706
01:02:36.757 --> 01:02:38.465
Uncle Rob!

707
01:02:38.717 --> 01:02:40.295
Aunt Georgette!

708
01:03:02.115 --> 01:03:04.737
(MUMBLES)

709
01:03:23.762 --> 01:03:25.838
Watch it, kid!

710
01:03:26.098 --> 01:03:28.137
(MAN CACKLES)

711
01:03:32.437 --> 01:03:35.604
You looking for someone
to read you a bedtime story?

712
01:03:35.858 --> 01:03:38.349
(WOMEN LAUGHING)

713
01:03:41.655 --> 01:03:43.030
Taxi!

714
01:03:56.003 --> 01:03:58.161
It's scary out there.

715
01:03:59.882 --> 01:04:01.257
Ain't much better in here.

716
01:04:01.508 --> 01:04:02.539
(GASPS)

717
01:04:28.952 --> 01:04:31.823
I don't ever want to take a vacation
like this again.

718
01:04:43.383 --> 01:04:45.459
(WINGS FLAPPING)

719
01:05:02.736 --> 01:05:04.111
KEVIN:
Where did you come from?

720
01:05:04.363 --> 01:05:06.106
I don't have enough for everybody.

721
01:05:06.448 --> 01:05:08.737
How hungry are you guys?

722
01:05:10.369 --> 01:05:12.445
You guys ate all my food.

723
01:05:27.678 --> 01:05:29.754
(SCREAMS)

724
01:06:11.763 --> 01:06:16.591
I'm sorry I screamed in your face.
You were trying to help me, right?

725
01:06:20.189 --> 01:06:22.015
I'm Kevin McCallister.

726
01:06:22.900 --> 01:06:24.358
Your birds are real nice.

727
01:06:25.694 --> 01:06:27.069
I've seen you before.

728
01:06:27.321 --> 01:06:29.397
You had pigeons all over you.

729
01:06:29.656 --> 01:06:33.950
At first, you look scary, but when
I think about it, it's not so bad.

730
01:06:34.244 --> 01:06:36.782
They must like you to be all over you.

731
01:06:38.540 --> 01:06:40.912
If I'm bothering you, I can leave.

732
01:06:41.168 --> 01:06:42.579
Am I bothering you?

733
01:06:44.129 --> 01:06:45.374
No.

734
01:06:46.298 --> 01:06:48.623
Good. I'm not a pain in the butt?

735
01:06:50.969 --> 01:06:52.167
No.

736
01:06:56.683 --> 01:06:59.601
Will the pigeons come back
on their own or do you call them?

737
01:07:11.240 --> 01:07:12.200
LAD Y:
Give me your hand.

738
01:07:15.410 --> 01:07:16.406
(GRAIN SPILLING)

739
01:07:16.662 --> 01:07:18.286
They can hear it.

740
01:07:35.597 --> 01:07:36.842
This is great!

741
01:07:41.144 --> 01:07:42.555
It's pretty cold out.

742
01:07:42.813 --> 01:07:46.478
I'd sure like a cup of hot chocolate.
How about you?

743
01:07:46.692 --> 01:07:47.522
My treat.

744
01:07:52.489 --> 01:07:55.158
KEVIN: I'd hate to spend Christmas Eve
in such a park.

745
01:07:55.409 --> 01:07:57.366
Can we go someplace warm?

746
01:07:57.744 --> 01:07:58.693
LAD Y:
Yes.

747
01:07:58.912 --> 01:08:00.371
I know a place.

748
01:08:03.458 --> 01:08:06.993
(ORCHESTRA PLAYS)

749
01:08:08.088 --> 01:08:12.086
(ORCHESTRA PLAYS
"O COME ALL YE FAITHFUL")

750
01:08:47.377 --> 01:08:49.287
Nice music.

751
01:08:50.714 --> 01:08:52.790
This place is great.

752
01:08:53.217 --> 01:08:56.004
LAD Y: I've heard the world's
great music from here.

753
01:08:57.846 --> 01:09:00.088
Ella Fitzgerald. Count Basie.

754
01:09:00.349 --> 01:09:02.057
Frank Sinatra.

755
01:09:02.392 --> 01:09:04.468
Luciano Pavarotti.

756
01:09:09.650 --> 01:09:11.441
Do you bring your friends here?

757
01:09:13.654 --> 01:09:15.196
I haven't got many friends.

758
01:09:16.323 --> 01:09:17.568
Sorry.

759
01:09:18.325 --> 01:09:20.483
I'm like the birds I care for.

760
01:09:21.411 --> 01:09:25.539
People pass me in the street.
They see me but they try to ignore me.

761
01:09:25.791 --> 01:09:27.867
They prefer I wasn't in their city.

762
01:09:28.418 --> 01:09:33.294
Yeah. It's like that with my family.
I'm like the pigeon of the house...

763
01:09:33.549 --> 01:09:35.091
just because I'm the youngest.

764
01:09:36.009 --> 01:09:38.085
Everyone fights for position.

765
01:09:38.470 --> 01:09:40.130
Everyone wants to be seen...

766
01:09:40.389 --> 01:09:41.338
and heard.

767
01:09:41.890 --> 01:09:42.969
I guess so.

768
01:09:43.225 --> 01:09:47.686
I'm seen and heard pretty much.
But I get sent to my room a lot too.

769
01:09:50.607 --> 01:09:52.766
I wasn't always like this.

770
01:09:53.402 --> 01:09:55.394
What were you like before?

771
01:09:56.113 --> 01:09:58.782
I had a job. I had a home.

772
01:09:59.324 --> 01:10:01.531
- I had a family.
- Any kids?

773
01:10:03.078 --> 01:10:04.241
No.

774
01:10:05.122 --> 01:10:06.782
I wanted them.

775
01:10:07.457 --> 01:10:10.957
But the man I loved
fell out of love with me.

776
01:10:11.920 --> 01:10:13.083
That broke my heart.

777
01:10:14.006 --> 01:10:16.544
When the chance
to be loved came along again...

778
01:10:17.634 --> 01:10:19.461
I ran away from it.

779
01:10:20.179 --> 01:10:21.970
I stopped trusting people.

780
01:10:22.514 --> 01:10:26.346
No offense, but that seems like
sort of a dumb thing to do.

781
01:10:26.768 --> 01:10:29.473
I was afraid of getting
my heart broken again.

782
01:10:30.105 --> 01:10:32.513
Sometimes you can trust a person...

783
01:10:32.774 --> 01:10:36.558
and then, when things are down,
they forget about you.

784
01:10:37.487 --> 01:10:39.279
Maybe they're just too busy.

785
01:10:39.531 --> 01:10:43.280
Maybe they don't forget about you,
but they forget to remember you.

786
01:10:43.535 --> 01:10:45.444
People don't mean to forget.

787
01:10:45.704 --> 01:10:47.364
My grandfather says...

788
01:10:47.623 --> 01:10:51.870
if my head wasn't screwed on,
I'd leave it on the school bus.

789
01:10:52.419 --> 01:10:56.120
I'm just afraid if I do trust someone,
I'll get my heart broken.

790
01:10:56.590 --> 01:10:57.669
I understand.

791
01:10:58.091 --> 01:11:00.464
I had a nice pair of Rollerblades.

792
01:11:00.719 --> 01:11:03.008
I was afraid to wreck them...

793
01:11:03.263 --> 01:11:06.928
so I kept them in a box.
Do you know what happened?

794
01:11:07.184 --> 01:11:11.976
I outgrew them. I never wore them
outside. Only in my room a few times.

795
01:11:13.482 --> 01:11:17.100
A person's heart and feelings
are very different than skates.

796
01:11:17.945 --> 01:11:19.984
They're kind of the same thing.

797
01:11:20.239 --> 01:11:23.323
If you won't use your heart,
who cares if it gets broken?

798
01:11:23.909 --> 01:11:27.527
If you just keep it to yourself,
maybe it'll be like my Rollerblades.

799
01:11:27.871 --> 01:11:31.240
When you do decide to try it,
it won't be any good.

800
01:11:31.500 --> 01:11:34.252
You should take a chance.
Got nothing to lose.

801
01:11:35.629 --> 01:11:37.669
Little truth in there somewhere.

802
01:11:37.923 --> 01:11:42.336
I think so. Your heart might
still be broken, but it isn't gone.

803
01:11:42.594 --> 01:11:44.883
If it was gone,
you wouldn't be so nice.

804
01:11:46.306 --> 01:11:47.469
Thank you.

805
01:11:49.726 --> 01:11:51.636
Do you know it's been...

806
01:11:52.729 --> 01:11:55.647
a couple of years
since I've talked to anybody?

807
01:11:56.024 --> 01:11:57.934
That's okay. You're good at it.

808
01:11:58.193 --> 01:12:00.863
You're not boring.
You don't mumble or spit.

809
01:12:01.113 --> 01:12:02.821
You should do it more often.

810
01:12:03.073 --> 01:12:06.323
Just wear an outfit
with no pigeon poop on it.

811
01:12:06.535 --> 01:12:08.444
(LAUGHS)

812
01:12:09.788 --> 01:12:13.038
I have been working very hard
at keeping people away.

813
01:12:13.292 --> 01:12:15.865
I always think I'll have
a lot of fun if I'm alone...

814
01:12:16.128 --> 01:12:18.500
but when I'm alone, it's not fun.

815
01:12:19.047 --> 01:12:21.621
I don't care how much people bug me...

816
01:12:21.884 --> 01:12:24.339
I'd rather be with someone
than alone.

817
01:12:25.387 --> 01:12:28.341
So what are you doing alone
on Christmas Eve?

818
01:12:28.891 --> 01:12:30.349
Did you get into trouble?

819
01:12:31.351 --> 01:12:32.300
Yeah.

820
01:12:32.519 --> 01:12:33.930
You did something wrong?

821
01:12:34.188 --> 01:12:35.563
A lot of things.

822
01:12:38.025 --> 01:12:41.643
Did you know that a good deed
erases a bad deed?

823
01:12:41.987 --> 01:12:44.656
It's late. I don't know
if I'll have enough time...

824
01:12:44.907 --> 01:12:47.907
to do enough good deeds
to erase all my bad ones.

825
01:12:48.285 --> 01:12:51.535
It's Christmas Eve.
Good deeds count extra tonight.

826
01:12:51.788 --> 01:12:54.458
- They do?
- Of course they do.

827
01:12:54.708 --> 01:12:58.492
Think of an important
thing you can do for others...

828
01:12:58.879 --> 01:13:00.124
and go do it.

829
01:13:00.839 --> 01:13:03.544
Just follow the star in your heart.

830
01:13:05.511 --> 01:13:06.709
Okay.

831
01:13:07.596 --> 01:13:10.265
It's getting pretty late.
I'd better get going.

832
01:13:17.523 --> 01:13:20.808
If I don't see you, I hope
everything turns out okay.

833
01:13:21.193 --> 01:13:22.687
Thank you.

834
01:13:23.237 --> 01:13:24.945
Tell the birds I said goodbye.

835
01:13:25.280 --> 01:13:26.561
I will.

836
01:13:34.831 --> 01:13:35.946
Merry Christmas.

837
01:13:36.333 --> 01:13:37.412
Merry Christmas.

838
01:13:37.835 --> 01:13:41.038
If you need somebody to trust,
it can be me.

839
01:13:41.296 --> 01:13:43.205
I won't forget to remember you.

840
01:13:44.258 --> 01:13:46.796
Don't make promises you can't keep.

841
01:14:45.736 --> 01:14:47.645
MR. DUNCAN:
All the money in the registers...

842
01:14:47.863 --> 01:14:51.362
Mr. Duncan is gonna donate
to the Children 's Hospital.

843
01:14:51.992 --> 01:14:55.657
MARV: At midnight tonight,
we're hitting Duncan 's Toy Chest.

844
01:14:55.913 --> 01:15:00.871
You can mess with a lot of things, but
you can't mess with kids on Christmas.

845
01:17:21.517 --> 01:17:24.517
CONCIERGE: We'd like to offer you
a complimentary suite.

846
01:17:25.229 --> 01:17:27.684
It's a penthouse
with a view of the park.

847
01:17:27.940 --> 01:17:32.483
I think you'll find it satisfactory.
It was recently vacated by a countess.

848
01:17:33.070 --> 01:17:35.857
What kind of hotel lets a child
check in alone?

849
01:17:36.198 --> 01:17:38.440
The boy had a very convincing story.

850
01:17:38.784 --> 01:17:40.907
What kind of idiots work here?

851
01:17:41.662 --> 01:17:43.701
The finest in New York.

852
01:17:44.373 --> 01:17:46.828
When you learned the credit card...

853
01:17:47.125 --> 01:17:49.035
I made the discovery.

854
01:17:49.294 --> 01:17:50.623
Why did you let him leave?

855
01:17:51.630 --> 01:17:53.623
We confronted him and he ran!

856
01:17:53.882 --> 01:17:54.878
You scared him!

857
01:17:55.217 --> 01:17:59.546
It's Christmas Eve, and because of you,
our child is lost in a huge city.

858
01:18:03.600 --> 01:18:05.926
Take our family and luggage
up to the room.

859
01:18:06.186 --> 01:18:07.217
Yes, sir!

860
01:18:07.437 --> 01:18:08.813
Run along, Cedric.

861
01:18:09.273 --> 01:18:12.689
I'll go to the police station to make
sure they're looking for Kevin.

862
01:18:12.943 --> 01:18:14.651
I want you to stay here.

863
01:18:14.903 --> 01:18:17.062
- I'm going to look for him.
- What?

864
01:18:17.322 --> 01:18:21.367
With all due respect, your son is lost
in one of the world's biggest cities.

865
01:18:22.703 --> 01:18:24.494
Could you stay out of this?

866
01:18:25.122 --> 01:18:26.153
As you wish.

867
01:18:26.707 --> 01:18:31.452
Thank you. It's not a good idea
to run around New York City alone.

868
01:18:31.712 --> 01:18:33.336
If Kevin can, so can I.

869
01:18:33.589 --> 01:18:34.668
- Kate...
- I'll be fine.

870
01:18:34.923 --> 01:18:37.841
The way I feel, no mugger
or murderer would mess with me.

871
01:18:40.053 --> 01:18:43.387
There are hundreds of armed
parasites out there!

872
01:18:45.475 --> 01:18:48.227
Do bundle up.
It's awfully cold outside.

873
01:18:53.817 --> 01:18:57.518
(CLOCK CHIMES)

874
01:19:23.013 --> 01:19:24.092
Marv. Marv.

875
01:19:24.348 --> 01:19:26.056
Come on, let's go.

876
01:19:46.745 --> 01:19:47.824
Marv.

877
01:19:48.080 --> 01:19:49.823
Crowbars up!

878
01:19:55.712 --> 01:19:57.705
Merry Christmas, Harry!

879
01:20:01.927 --> 01:20:04.335
Happy Hanukkah, Marv!

880
01:20:13.981 --> 01:20:16.816
MARV: This is more money
than I can even count!

881
01:20:17.067 --> 01:20:21.314
It makes you wonder why we spent
so much time robbing homes.

882
01:20:34.918 --> 01:20:37.836
The amazing thing is,
we're fugitives from the law...

883
01:20:38.088 --> 01:20:42.133
we're up to our elbows in cash
and nobody even knows about it.

884
01:20:42.885 --> 01:20:43.964
(KNOCKS)

885
01:20:46.680 --> 01:20:48.008
He's back!

886
01:20:49.558 --> 01:20:50.756
He took our picture!

887
01:20:51.018 --> 01:20:52.298
How was my hair?

888
01:20:58.525 --> 01:21:01.977
This is it. No turning back.

889
01:21:02.404 --> 01:21:04.895
Another Christmas in the trenches.

890
01:21:06.325 --> 01:21:07.902
No!

891
01:21:12.539 --> 01:21:13.654
(ALARM BELL RINGS)

892
01:21:13.874 --> 01:21:14.739
Wow.

893
01:21:15.000 --> 01:21:17.206
That's it! Get the money!
Get it!

894
01:21:19.046 --> 01:21:20.588
(MUMBLES)

895
01:21:23.258 --> 01:21:24.587
I'll kill him!

896
01:21:27.095 --> 01:21:29.135
- Marv!
- I'm coming, Harry!

897
01:21:30.599 --> 01:21:33.220
(HARRY YELLS)

898
01:21:38.357 --> 01:21:39.637
Harry?

899
01:21:40.025 --> 01:21:41.852
(GROANS)

900
01:21:42.444 --> 01:21:43.689
Harry!

901
01:21:44.279 --> 01:21:45.358
That was incredible.

902
01:21:46.740 --> 01:21:47.903
(MUMBLES)

903
01:21:49.201 --> 01:21:51.906
- I twisted my ankle.
- Where is he?

904
01:21:52.162 --> 01:21:54.369
Hey, guys! Smile!

905
01:21:57.084 --> 01:21:58.364
Come on! Come on!

906
01:21:58.836 --> 01:22:00.495
- Help me.
- I got you.

907
01:22:00.921 --> 01:22:02.296
I got you.

908
01:22:29.533 --> 01:22:31.027
Taxi!

909
01:22:36.540 --> 01:22:38.117
Times Square!

910
01:22:59.855 --> 01:23:01.266
Where'd he go?

911
01:23:02.399 --> 01:23:03.977
KEVIN:
I'm up here! Come get me!

912
01:23:06.695 --> 01:23:07.644
Let's kill!

913
01:23:07.905 --> 01:23:09.613
Hold on, pea-brain.

914
01:23:09.865 --> 01:23:13.613
We got busted because we underestimated
that bundle of misery.

915
01:23:13.869 --> 01:23:15.114
This ain't like that.

916
01:23:15.579 --> 01:23:19.826
This ain't his house. The kid's
running scared. He ain't got a plan.

917
01:23:20.334 --> 01:23:23.003
May I do the thinking, please?

918
01:23:24.171 --> 01:23:25.333
Thank you.

919
01:23:27.633 --> 01:23:28.498
Sonny!

920
01:23:28.884 --> 01:23:30.082
Yes?

921
01:23:30.427 --> 01:23:34.092
Nothing would thrill me
more greatly than to shoot you.

922
01:23:34.598 --> 01:23:37.718
Knocking off a youngster
won't mean that much to me.

923
01:23:37.976 --> 01:23:39.352
- Understand?
- Mm-hm.

924
01:23:39.853 --> 01:23:43.305
But since we're in a hurry,
I'll make a deal with you.

925
01:23:43.690 --> 01:23:47.391
You throw down your camera
and we won't hurt you.

926
01:23:48.403 --> 01:23:52.235
You'll never hear from us again.
Okay?

927
01:23:52.574 --> 01:23:53.570
Promise?

928
01:23:54.409 --> 01:23:57.825
I cross my heart and hope to die.

929
01:23:58.664 --> 01:24:00.288
Okay!

930
01:24:05.712 --> 01:24:07.041
Okay, kid...

931
01:24:07.506 --> 01:24:09.048
give it to me.

932
01:24:17.391 --> 01:24:18.387
Direct hit!

933
01:24:24.398 --> 01:24:26.556
How many fingers am I holding up?

934
01:24:29.278 --> 01:24:30.309
Eight?

935
01:24:33.740 --> 01:24:37.608
Okay, kid. You want to throw bricks?
Go ahead, throw another one.

936
01:24:38.120 --> 01:24:39.697
MARV:
Don't do that!

937
01:24:39.913 --> 01:24:40.992
(YELPS)

938
01:24:43.333 --> 01:24:46.749
If you can't do any better than that,
you're going to lose.

939
01:24:48.380 --> 01:24:49.874
Harry...

940
01:24:50.299 --> 01:24:51.330
no.

941
01:24:53.552 --> 01:24:55.379
(YELPS)

942
01:24:57.764 --> 01:24:59.722
You got any more?

943
01:25:02.269 --> 01:25:04.760
Get up.
He don't have any more bricks.

944
01:25:10.819 --> 01:25:11.685
(MUMBLES)

945
01:25:11.904 --> 01:25:13.066
What?

946
01:25:13.655 --> 01:25:14.569
(MUMBLES)

947
01:25:14.907 --> 01:25:16.187
What?

948
01:25:16.408 --> 01:25:17.783
(MUMBLES)

949
01:25:18.327 --> 01:25:19.785
What?

950
01:25:20.829 --> 01:25:21.825
(YELPS)

951
01:25:22.539 --> 01:25:26.371
That did it! Nobody throws bricks
at me and gets away with it. Come on!

952
01:25:26.627 --> 01:25:28.915
You go this way. I'll go around back.

953
01:25:33.258 --> 01:25:34.966
Harry?

954
01:25:36.303 --> 01:25:38.094
Harry?

955
01:25:38.931 --> 01:25:41.422
Harry?

956
01:26:04.665 --> 01:26:05.827
Huh?

957
01:26:31.066 --> 01:26:34.067
(SCREAMS)

958
01:26:39.783 --> 01:26:42.239
(MUMBLES)

959
01:26:53.964 --> 01:26:54.913
(YELPS)

960
01:27:00.262 --> 01:27:02.883
(MUMBLES)

961
01:27:07.227 --> 01:27:09.101
(LAUGHS)

962
01:27:27.164 --> 01:27:28.195
(YELLS)

963
01:27:34.963 --> 01:27:36.956
(MUMBLES)

964
01:27:45.390 --> 01:27:47.383
(GROWLS)

965
01:28:06.870 --> 01:28:08.246
Harry!

966
01:28:08.580 --> 01:28:10.537
I reached the top!

967
01:28:12.292 --> 01:28:13.751
(YELLS)

968
01:28:18.966 --> 01:28:22.299
(CRACKS NECK)

969
01:28:25.222 --> 01:28:26.385
Ahh.

970
01:28:29.142 --> 01:28:31.550
(MUMBLES)

971
01:28:55.544 --> 01:28:57.168
(RATTLES DOORKNOB)

972
01:29:02.926 --> 01:29:05.215
You better do better than this.

973
01:29:10.601 --> 01:29:11.431
(GROANS)

974
01:29:11.685 --> 01:29:12.800
(WRENCH CONKS HARRY)

975
01:29:28.076 --> 01:29:29.357
(CRACKS BACK)

976
01:29:29.870 --> 01:29:31.447
Wow!

977
01:29:31.705 --> 01:29:33.532
What a hole!

978
01:29:54.895 --> 01:29:55.808
Whoa!

979
01:30:09.576 --> 01:30:11.035
(SCREAMS)

980
01:30:13.038 --> 01:30:13.868
Uh-oh.

981
01:30:20.295 --> 01:30:22.418
(MUMBLES)

982
01:30:42.359 --> 01:30:43.224
Ah!

983
01:31:03.505 --> 01:31:05.083
(SCREAMS)

984
01:31:46.423 --> 01:31:48.250
(SCREAMS)

985
01:32:33.178 --> 01:32:34.756
(CHUCKLES)

986
01:32:45.858 --> 01:32:48.265
(SCREAMS)

987
01:32:59.580 --> 01:33:02.071
(GLASS BREAKS)

988
01:33:09.047 --> 01:33:11.621
(SIZZLES)

989
01:33:17.764 --> 01:33:21.430
(WHIMPERS)

990
01:33:41.163 --> 01:33:42.954
Harry.

991
01:34:03.644 --> 01:34:05.470
I'm coming up!

992
01:34:11.068 --> 01:34:12.562
Uh-oh.

993
01:34:20.160 --> 01:34:22.402
I'm gonna murder that kid!

994
01:34:23.997 --> 01:34:26.073
(SNEEZES)

995
01:34:40.472 --> 01:34:41.717
Yes!

996
01:34:48.689 --> 01:34:49.887
Whoa.

997
01:34:58.657 --> 01:35:01.148
Whoa, whoa!

998
01:35:02.494 --> 01:35:03.869
(YELPS)

999
01:35:11.670 --> 01:35:12.833
MARV:
Hey!

1000
01:35:13.172 --> 01:35:16.007
Don't you know a kid always wins
against two idiots?

1001
01:35:16.258 --> 01:35:18.500
Harry! In the living room!

1002
01:35:18.760 --> 01:35:19.840
(MUMBLES)

1003
01:35:20.095 --> 01:35:21.720
He went up the ladder!

1004
01:35:31.648 --> 01:35:33.273
(YELLS)

1005
01:35:36.695 --> 01:35:38.273
Oh.

1006
01:35:39.281 --> 01:35:40.989
I'm coming, Harry.

1007
01:35:41.575 --> 01:35:42.690
I'm coming.

1008
01:35:47.915 --> 01:35:49.113
Harry!

1009
01:35:51.168 --> 01:35:55.000
You didn't lose any teeth!
Come on, he went to the second floor.

1010
01:35:55.506 --> 01:35:56.419
Hey!

1011
01:35:56.632 --> 01:35:57.960
Try the stairs.

1012
01:35:58.800 --> 01:36:00.259
Right.

1013
01:36:03.180 --> 01:36:04.971
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

1014
01:36:05.390 --> 01:36:06.671
Remember last year?

1015
01:36:08.018 --> 01:36:08.848
No.

1016
01:36:09.478 --> 01:36:11.221
Watch this.

1017
01:36:11.688 --> 01:36:13.515
Let's get him!

1018
01:36:13.732 --> 01:36:15.191
(STOMPS)

1019
01:36:17.569 --> 01:36:18.518
Ow!

1020
01:36:18.737 --> 01:36:21.857
He busted me right in my mouth, Marv!

1021
01:36:22.282 --> 01:36:23.231
That's one.

1022
01:36:24.034 --> 01:36:25.576
Don't worry, Harry.

1023
01:36:26.828 --> 01:36:28.620
I'll get him.

1024
01:36:28.830 --> 01:36:29.660
(STOMPS)

1025
01:36:33.377 --> 01:36:34.372
Ow!

1026
01:36:35.254 --> 01:36:37.495
Right in the schnoz.

1027
01:36:38.507 --> 01:36:39.621
That's two.

1028
01:36:39.883 --> 01:36:41.425
Come on, let's get him.

1029
01:36:44.471 --> 01:36:45.301
MARV:
Oops.

1030
01:36:46.223 --> 01:36:47.765
(YELLING)

1031
01:36:53.272 --> 01:36:54.517
That's...

1032
01:36:54.773 --> 01:36:56.102
three.

1033
01:37:01.905 --> 01:37:03.020
No.

1034
01:37:03.240 --> 01:37:05.031
(PIPE CRASHES)

1035
01:37:05.242 --> 01:37:07.235
MARV:
That's four.

1036
01:37:12.124 --> 01:37:15.244
- Come on, Harry.
- Marv, are you sure this is safe?

1037
01:37:16.503 --> 01:37:18.662
I've worked all the kinks out.

1038
01:37:18.922 --> 01:37:20.381
Solid as a rock.

1039
01:37:33.979 --> 01:37:36.185
(CRASHING)

1040
01:37:37.482 --> 01:37:39.689
Like a rock, huh?

1041
01:37:39.943 --> 01:37:40.857
Give up?

1042
01:37:41.195 --> 01:37:44.445
KEVIN: Have you had enough pain?
- Never!

1043
01:37:55.751 --> 01:37:58.456
You better say every prayer
you ever heard!

1044
01:37:58.712 --> 01:38:01.250
I hope your parents got you
a tombstone for Christmas.

1045
01:38:04.092 --> 01:38:05.421
Where'd he go?

1046
01:38:05.677 --> 01:38:08.299
I'm up here and I'm really scared.

1047
01:38:18.190 --> 01:38:19.898
What's that sound?

1048
01:38:20.108 --> 01:38:21.188
(CLATTERING)

1049
01:38:29.618 --> 01:38:30.697
(YELLING)

1050
01:38:39.920 --> 01:38:42.411
That was the sound of a tool chest...

1051
01:38:42.673 --> 01:38:45.164
falling down the stairs.

1052
01:38:45.384 --> 01:38:46.582
Oh.

1053
01:38:48.470 --> 01:38:50.214
(CRACKING NOSES)

1054
01:38:51.139 --> 01:38:52.634
Yes!

1055
01:39:27.676 --> 01:39:29.051
Over there!

1056
01:39:29.428 --> 01:39:32.263
Even if I get the chair,
I'm killing that kid!

1057
01:39:35.017 --> 01:39:36.594
Surrender, kid!

1058
01:39:37.227 --> 01:39:38.057
He vanished.

1059
01:39:38.312 --> 01:39:40.020
I'm here, you horse's ass!

1060
01:39:44.109 --> 01:39:44.939
Whoa.

1061
01:39:45.194 --> 01:39:46.688
Nice night for a neck injury!

1062
01:39:48.488 --> 01:39:51.110
Suck brick, kid!

1063
01:39:56.830 --> 01:39:58.739
Come on, Marv.

1064
01:39:59.166 --> 01:40:00.079
I don't know.

1065
01:40:00.334 --> 01:40:02.243
I said, come on!

1066
01:40:03.879 --> 01:40:06.037
HARRY:
Come on, you big sissy.

1067
01:40:06.298 --> 01:40:07.876
(WHIMPERS)

1068
01:40:20.103 --> 01:40:22.641
Harry? You wearing aftershave?

1069
01:40:22.981 --> 01:40:24.689
That's kerosene.

1070
01:40:25.484 --> 01:40:27.726
The rope is soaked in it.

1071
01:40:27.986 --> 01:40:30.524
Why would anyone soak a rope
in kerosene?

1072
01:40:35.494 --> 01:40:37.570
Merry Christmas.

1073
01:40:37.788 --> 01:40:38.618
Go up!

1074
01:40:38.872 --> 01:40:40.035
(SCREAMS)

1075
01:41:06.984 --> 01:41:09.522
(SCREAMING)

1076
01:41:14.283 --> 01:41:15.907
Get off me!

1077
01:41:16.159 --> 01:41:17.535
(SCREAMING)

1078
01:41:39.141 --> 01:41:40.718
Get the bag!

1079
01:41:41.393 --> 01:41:44.429
Two guys who robbed Duncan's Toy Chest
are in the park.

1080
01:41:44.688 --> 01:41:49.599
Central Park West, 95th Street. Look
for fireworks. Hurry, they got a gun.

1081
01:41:55.949 --> 01:41:57.028
KEVIN:
I'm here.

1082
01:41:57.284 --> 01:42:00.368
Better come and get me
before I call the cops.

1083
01:42:04.166 --> 01:42:05.446
(HONKS)

1084
01:42:07.753 --> 01:42:08.915
Whoa!

1085
01:42:15.385 --> 01:42:18.137
My, how the tables have turned.

1086
01:42:18.388 --> 01:42:19.847
HARRY:
How do you like the ice?

1087
01:42:20.849 --> 01:42:22.758
(LAUGHING)

1088
01:42:25.604 --> 01:42:28.558
Let's go for a little stroll
in the park.

1089
01:42:45.749 --> 01:42:46.745
HARRY:
Give me the bag.

1090
01:42:47.042 --> 01:42:48.501
Give me it!

1091
01:42:53.382 --> 01:42:55.505
Great for the album.

1092
01:42:56.510 --> 01:43:00.175
You may've won the battle, dude,
but you lost the war.

1093
01:43:01.056 --> 01:43:02.965
You ought not of messed with us.

1094
01:43:03.475 --> 01:43:04.471
We're dangerous.

1095
01:43:09.481 --> 01:43:10.430
(WINGS FLAPPING)

1096
01:43:10.899 --> 01:43:12.559
- Harry?
- Shut up!

1097
01:43:17.239 --> 01:43:18.104
Harry.

1098
01:43:18.574 --> 01:43:20.899
HARRY:
Shut up! I want to enjoy this.

1099
01:43:21.827 --> 01:43:23.451
MARV:
Something's wrong.

1100
01:43:24.079 --> 01:43:26.155
- Let's get out of here!
- Shut up!

1101
01:43:28.417 --> 01:43:30.409
HARRY:
I never made it to the 6th grade...

1102
01:43:31.378 --> 01:43:34.379
and it doesn't look like
you're gonna either.

1103
01:43:35.465 --> 01:43:36.924
Let him go!

1104
01:43:37.259 --> 01:43:38.634
Kevin, run!

1105
01:43:40.512 --> 01:43:41.888
Shoot her!

1106
01:43:42.097 --> 01:43:43.757
Shoot her!

1107
01:43:44.016 --> 01:43:45.925
- Shoot her!
- I'm trying!

1108
01:43:58.405 --> 01:44:00.445
(SCREAMING)

1109
01:44:24.431 --> 01:44:25.890
(LAUGHS)

1110
01:44:26.141 --> 01:44:27.220
Bye! Thanks.

1111
01:44:48.121 --> 01:44:50.197
(SIRENS)

1112
01:44:53.877 --> 01:44:56.547
COP 1:
Jesus, looks like the 4th of July!

1113
01:44:57.256 --> 01:44:59.213
We got the bridge.
Take the tunnel.

1114
01:44:59.466 --> 01:45:00.841
COP 2:
Let's go, let's go!

1115
01:45:04.805 --> 01:45:06.133
(MARV WHIMPERS)

1116
01:45:06.390 --> 01:45:08.513
(HARRY MUMBLES)

1117
01:45:08.767 --> 01:45:10.226
Oh, my God!

1118
01:45:11.186 --> 01:45:12.645
(GUNSHOT)

1119
01:45:21.029 --> 01:45:22.227
COP 2:
All right, let's go.

1120
01:45:22.489 --> 01:45:24.197
COP 1:
Come on, on your feet.

1121
01:45:29.037 --> 01:45:33.699
You guys should've started earlier.
The prisoners already exchanged gifts.

1122
01:45:33.959 --> 01:45:35.584
We missed the presents?

1123
01:45:35.836 --> 01:45:39.419
He made us hide in the store
and steal the kiddies' charity money.

1124
01:45:39.673 --> 01:45:41.547
Shut up, Marv.

1125
01:45:43.427 --> 01:45:45.550
HARRY:
You've got the right to remain silent.

1126
01:45:45.971 --> 01:45:48.925
He's a little cranky.
We just broke out of prison.

1127
01:45:49.183 --> 01:45:50.974
Shut up, Marv!

1128
01:45:52.060 --> 01:45:53.804
Get them out of here!

1129
01:45:54.062 --> 01:45:55.521
If this makes the papers...

1130
01:45:55.772 --> 01:45:59.307
we're no longer the Wet Bandits,
we're the Sticky Bandits.

1131
01:46:00.360 --> 01:46:01.558
MARV:
That's sticky. S...

1132
01:46:02.696 --> 01:46:04.107
T...

1133
01:46:04.698 --> 01:46:06.276
HARRY: I.
MARV: I.

1134
01:46:18.420 --> 01:46:21.955
COP: It's all over. We apprehended
the thieves and got your money.

1135
01:46:22.216 --> 01:46:25.585
MR. DUNCAN: I want to get that money
over to the Children's Hospital.

1136
01:46:25.802 --> 01:46:28.507
COP: I'll handle it.
MR. DUNCAN: Thank you.

1137
01:46:29.306 --> 01:46:30.551
Excuse me.

1138
01:46:30.891 --> 01:46:34.474
I found this note. Looks like
a kid broke your window.

1139
01:46:35.187 --> 01:46:36.432
KEVIN:
Dear Mr. Duncan:

1140
01:46:36.688 --> 01:46:39.476
I broke your window
to catch the bad guys.

1141
01:46:39.733 --> 01:46:41.227
Do you have insurance?

1142
01:46:41.485 --> 01:46:44.936
If not, I'll send you some money,
if I ever get home.

1143
01:46:45.197 --> 01:46:47.154
Merry Christmas.
Kevin McCallister.

1144
01:46:47.491 --> 01:46:50.196
P. S. Thanks for the turtledoves.

1145
01:46:51.411 --> 01:46:53.071
Turtledoves.

1146
01:46:54.248 --> 01:46:55.410
Oh.

1147
01:47:02.756 --> 01:47:05.461
Excuse me. I'm looking for my son.
This boy here.

1148
01:47:08.303 --> 01:47:12.218
Please help me. This boy right here.
Have you seen him?

1149
01:47:17.229 --> 01:47:18.059
(KNOCKS)

1150
01:47:21.358 --> 01:47:24.774
I'm looking for my son.
He's been missing for two days.

1151
01:47:25.028 --> 01:47:27.863
- Have you filed a report?
- Of course we have.

1152
01:47:29.825 --> 01:47:32.494
Then trust us. We'll handle it.

1153
01:47:34.288 --> 01:47:35.450
Oh.

1154
01:47:37.541 --> 01:47:38.537
I'm his mother.

1155
01:47:40.252 --> 01:47:42.921
I know, but you're looking
for a needle in a haystack.

1156
01:47:44.423 --> 01:47:45.585
Do you have kids?

1157
01:47:46.925 --> 01:47:47.755
Yes, ma'am.

1158
01:47:48.051 --> 01:47:49.759
What if one was missing?

1159
01:47:52.347 --> 01:47:54.838
I'd probably do the same thing
you're doing.

1160
01:47:56.185 --> 01:47:57.264
Thank you.

1161
01:48:00.022 --> 01:48:01.813
Put yourself in his shoes.

1162
01:48:02.232 --> 01:48:04.141
What would you do?

1163
01:48:04.401 --> 01:48:07.770
Me? I'd probably be lying dead
in a gutter somewhere.

1164
01:48:09.239 --> 01:48:10.698
But not Kevin.

1165
01:48:10.908 --> 01:48:14.573
No. Kevin is so much stronger
and braver than I am.

1166
01:48:15.495 --> 01:48:18.117
I know Kevin's fine. I'm sure he is.

1167
01:48:19.708 --> 01:48:22.377
But he's still alone in a big city.

1168
01:48:23.295 --> 01:48:25.086
He doesn't deserve that.

1169
01:48:25.339 --> 01:48:29.799
He deserves to be at home with his own
family around his Christmas tree.

1170
01:48:33.430 --> 01:48:34.805
Oh, dear God...

1171
01:48:35.724 --> 01:48:37.266
I know where he is.

1172
01:48:37.976 --> 01:48:40.550
I need to get to Rockefeller Center.

1173
01:48:40.812 --> 01:48:43.054
- Hop in.
- Thank you.

1174
01:48:47.361 --> 01:48:51.524
I know I don't deserve a Christmas
even if I did do a good deed.

1175
01:48:52.491 --> 01:48:54.033
I don't want any presents.

1176
01:48:54.368 --> 01:48:58.317
Instead, I want to take back every mean
thing I ever said to my family...

1177
01:48:58.580 --> 01:49:00.787
even if they don't do the same.

1178
01:49:01.375 --> 01:49:05.289
I don't care. I love all of them.
Including Buzz.

1179
01:49:06.380 --> 01:49:09.665
If I can't see all of them,
could I just see my mother?

1180
01:49:10.551 --> 01:49:14.631
I'll never want another thing, ever.
I just want my mother.

1181
01:49:15.222 --> 01:49:16.681
I know it won't be tonight...

1182
01:49:17.015 --> 01:49:21.060
but promise me I can see her again.
Sometime. Anytime.

1183
01:49:22.062 --> 01:49:25.431
Even if it's just once
and only for a few minutes.

1184
01:49:25.774 --> 01:49:28.063
I need to tell her I'm sorry.

1185
01:49:36.493 --> 01:49:37.868
Kevin?

1186
01:49:44.084 --> 01:49:44.914
Mom?

1187
01:49:47.629 --> 01:49:49.337
That worked fast!

1188
01:50:00.267 --> 01:50:01.726
Oh, Kevin.

1189
01:50:03.270 --> 01:50:04.930
Mom, I'm sorry.

1190
01:50:06.773 --> 01:50:08.398
I'm sorry too.

1191
01:50:20.996 --> 01:50:22.538
Merry Christmas, Mom.

1192
01:50:24.917 --> 01:50:26.993
Merry Christmas, sweetheart.

1193
01:50:28.504 --> 01:50:29.962
Thank you.

1194
01:50:30.631 --> 01:50:31.710
Let's go.

1195
01:50:32.633 --> 01:50:34.008
KEVIN:
How'd you know I was here?

1196
01:50:34.259 --> 01:50:37.011
KATE: I know you and Christmas trees,
and this is the biggest.

1197
01:50:37.262 --> 01:50:38.507
KEVIN:
Where's everyone else?

1198
01:50:38.764 --> 01:50:41.681
KATE: At the hotel.
They didn't like palm trees either.

1199
01:51:04.122 --> 01:51:06.696
(SNORING)

1200
01:51:25.769 --> 01:51:28.177
Holy smokes, it's morning!

1201
01:51:29.565 --> 01:51:31.890
FULLER:
It's Christmas morning, man.

1202
01:51:33.026 --> 01:51:35.019
Don't get your hopes up.

1203
01:51:35.571 --> 01:51:36.436
Huh?

1204
01:51:36.697 --> 01:51:38.570
I don't think Santa visits hotels.

1205
01:51:38.907 --> 01:51:41.114
Are you nuts? He's omnipresent.

1206
01:51:41.326 --> 01:51:42.821
He goes everywhere.

1207
01:51:44.663 --> 01:51:46.371
Wake up, it's Christmas!

1208
01:51:51.044 --> 01:51:53.286
Mom! Dad! It's Christmas!

1209
01:52:05.809 --> 01:52:07.303
BUZZ:
Wow.

1210
01:52:07.561 --> 01:52:09.020
ROD:
Where'd it come from?

1211
01:52:09.271 --> 01:52:11.727
KEVIN:
Mom! Dad! You gotta see this!

1212
01:52:15.569 --> 01:52:17.147
- My gosh!
- Peter!

1213
01:52:17.863 --> 01:52:19.772
BUZZ:
Are we in the right room?

1214
01:52:25.370 --> 01:52:27.030
Don't open any of mine.

1215
01:52:27.414 --> 01:52:30.166
- Who's Mr. Duncan?
- Duncan? I don't know.

1216
01:52:30.667 --> 01:52:31.996
Everybody calm down.

1217
01:52:32.336 --> 01:52:34.459
Calm down!

1218
01:52:35.214 --> 01:52:36.791
All right. Now...

1219
01:52:37.299 --> 01:52:40.917
if Kevin hadn't screwed up in
the first place, again...

1220
01:52:41.637 --> 01:52:44.210
we wouldn't be
in this most perfect...

1221
01:52:44.473 --> 01:52:47.178
and huge hotel room
with all this free stuff.

1222
01:52:47.976 --> 01:52:48.806
So...

1223
01:52:49.144 --> 01:52:52.643
I think it only fair that Kevin
get to open the first gift.

1224
01:52:54.066 --> 01:52:56.771
Then I'll go and the rest
of you and so on.

1225
01:53:01.323 --> 01:53:02.948
Merry Christmas, Kev.

1226
01:53:03.700 --> 01:53:05.693
Merry Christmas, Buzz.

1227
01:53:07.829 --> 01:53:09.372
Merry Christmas, Kevin.

1228
01:53:10.791 --> 01:53:12.914
All right! Merry Christmas!

1229
01:53:15.170 --> 01:53:16.201
Enough gooey sh...

1230
01:53:17.172 --> 01:53:19.842
Show of emotion.
Everyone, let's dig in!

1231
01:53:22.594 --> 01:53:26.592
LESLIE: Everybody, save the paper.
We can use it next year. And the bows.

1232
01:54:02.676 --> 01:54:04.503
Merry Christmas.

1233
01:54:06.722 --> 01:54:07.718
Kevin!

1234
01:54:07.931 --> 01:54:09.591
Merry Christmas!

1235
01:54:10.434 --> 01:54:11.762
I got something for you.

1236
01:54:20.277 --> 01:54:21.273
What's this?

1237
01:54:21.904 --> 01:54:24.655
It's a turtledove. I have one.
You have one.

1238
01:54:24.907 --> 01:54:28.691
As long as we each have a turtledove,
we'll be friends forever.

1239
01:54:32.706 --> 01:54:35.244
Oh, Kevin.

1240
01:54:38.045 --> 01:54:39.503
Thank you.

1241
01:54:40.964 --> 01:54:43.634
I won't forget you. Trust me.

1242
01:55:11.703 --> 01:55:13.696
The room service bill, sir.

1243
01:55:16.041 --> 01:55:17.416
Merry Christmas.

1244
01:55:18.710 --> 01:55:20.288
Uh, oh.

1245
01:55:24.007 --> 01:55:25.336
Nice family.

1246
01:55:25.592 --> 01:55:26.671
Really.

1247
01:55:36.019 --> 01:55:37.597
Merry Christmas indeed.

1248
01:55:41.441 --> 01:55:42.817
PETER:
Kevin!

1249
01:55:43.068 --> 01:55:45.855
You spent $967 on room service?!
